# Copy to .env for local Astro (PUBLIC_* only).
# Server secrets go in Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Environment variables.

# --- Contact form (recommended first — powers "Work with me" on /services) ---
# Free key at https://web3forms.com
# PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=your-key-here

# --- Stripe (optional — leave off until configured) ---
# Cloudflare Pages needs BOTH:
#   Build-time:  PUBLIC_STRIPE_CHECKOUT=true   (so the button is compiled into /services)
#   Runtime:     STRIPE_SECRET_KEY + STRIPE_PRICE_ID  (encrypted; used by /api/checkout)
# Price id must look like price_… (not prod_…). After changing PUBLIC_*, Retry deployment.
# PUBLIC_STRIPE_CHECKOUT=true
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_ID=price_...
# Test checkout locally: npm run build && npx wrangler pages dev ./dist

# --- Site sign-in: dream journal + comments (Google / GitHub) ---
# Runtime secrets (Functions). Exact names — do NOT reuse the /admin GITHUB_* below:
#   DREAM_SESSION_SECRET          (long random string; signs the session cookie)
#   DREAM_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID
#   DREAM_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
# GitHub OAuth App (developers → OAuth Apps, not GitHub Apps):
#      Homepage URL:               https://aditirk.me
#      Authorization callback URL: https://aditirk.me/api/dream-callback
# Client ID + secret must be from the SAME OAuth App. If GitHub says
# "client_id and/or client_secret passed are incorrect", regenerate the Client
# Secret on that app, paste into DREAM_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET, Save, then
# Deployments → Retry deployment (env changes need a redeploy).
# Handled by functions/api/dream-auth.ts + dream-callback.ts.

# --- Browser editing at /admin/ (Sveltia CMS + GitHub OAuth) ---
# Can share one OAuth App with dream sign-in if you add BOTH redirects:
#   https://aditirk.me/api/dream-callback
#   https://aditirk.me/api/callback
# Or use a separate OAuth App for admin only. Exact env names:
#   GITHUB_CLIENT_ID
#   GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET
# 1. github.com/settings/developers → OAuth Apps (not GitHub Apps)
#      Homepage URL:               https://aditirk.me
#      Authorization callback URL: https://aditirk.me/api/callback
#    Click "Update application" after editing. Copy Client ID + generate a Client Secret.
# 2. Cloudflare → Pages → your project → Settings → Variables and Secrets
#      Add both for Production (Encrypt the secret). Then Deployments → Retry deployment.
# 3. Open https://aditirk.me/admin/ → Login with GitHub (allow popups).
# Phones: the popup often opens as a separate tab and can't hand the login
# back. Use "Sign In with Token" on the /admin/ login screen instead — create a
# fine-grained token at github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens limited to
# this repo with Contents: Read and write. It stays signed in on that device.
# Local: astro dev → http://127.0.0.1:4321/admin/ → “Work with Local Repository”.
# Handled by functions/api/auth.ts + functions/api/callback.ts.
#
# Photos: CMS uploads are resized + converted to WebP in the browser (drops
# EXIF/GPS). Photos added by hand to public/photos: run `npm run photos:process`
# BEFORE committing — the build cleans the deployed copy, not git history.

# --- Quick thoughts from your phone (/quick) ---
# Post a thought from one textbox; it commits src/content/thoughts/<date>-<time>.md.
# On iPhone: open https://aditirk.me/quick in Safari → Share → Add to Home Screen.
#   GITHUB_CONTENT_TOKEN   fine-grained PAT, this repo only, Contents: Read and write (encrypted)
#   QUICK_POST_SUBS        comma-separated session ids allowed to post, e.g. google:1234…,github:5678
#                          (falls back to COMMENT_ADMIN_SUBS; find yours at /api/dream-session → "sub")
#   QUICK_POST_TOKEN       optional; lets an iOS Shortcut POST with "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
#   GITHUB_CONTENT_REPO    optional, default aditirk1/aditis-website
#   GITHUB_CONTENT_BRANCH  optional, default main

# --- Security headers ---
# public/_headers sets HSTS, X-Frame-Options, nosniff, Referrer-Policy,
# Permissions-Policy, and a Content-Security-Policy in *Report-Only* mode.
# Watch the browser console for CSP reports for a week; when clean, rename the
# header to Content-Security-Policy to enforce. If you turn on Umami, add its
# host to script-src and connect-src first.
# Rate limits (comments, checkout, admin, quick) use VISITOR_KV; they're skipped if it isn't bound.

# --- Visitor globe (Cloudflare Pages + KV; not used by astro dev alone) ---
# Create KV in Cloudflare, bind as VISITOR_KV in Pages + wrangler.toml.
# Set ADMIN_STATS_SECRET in Cloudflare (encrypted), not here — use /admin/visitors.
# VISITOR_COUNT_EPOCH: set/change this in Cloudflare Pages to zero the counter.
#   Any new value starts a clean count (e.g. 2026-09-07). Leave unset to keep totals.
# Your own browser: load /?visits=off once so your visits never count (/?visits=on undoes it).
# PUBLIC_VISITOR_API_BASE=

# --- Analytics (optional) ---
# PUBLIC_UMAMI_SCRIPT_URL=
# PUBLIC_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
